{"kind":"assert","text":"Cause of the Grow archive 400 found by a planner probe. The Artifacts host supports only the blob:none fetch filter. The Worker's v2 fetch sends filter tree:0.\n\nProbe (15:29 to 15:31 EDT): a scratch repository planner-probe/probe-v2fetch with two commits, on the same Artifacts host, with a repository token sent as a Bearer header from a file. The repository is now deleted and the token files are removed.\n- The v2 advertisement is: version 2, agent=gitty/1.0, ls-refs=unborn, fetch=shallow filter sideband-all, object-format=sha1. It names \"filter\" but not the filter kinds, so a capability check cannot detect this.\n- The exact Worker body (command=fetch, delimiter, want \u003cid\u003e, deepen 1, filter tree:0, no-progress, done) gives 400 text/plain \"Unsupported Git fetch filter; only blob:none is supported.\" The result is the same for the tip and the parent commit, with or without deepen 1, and with object-format=sha1 added.\n- Without the filter, the request gives 200 application/x-git-upload-pack-result: with deepen 1, shallow-info and then the packfile; without deepen, the packfile only.\n- With filter blob:none (with or without deepen 1), the request gives 200 and a pack of 2 objects for a root commit: the commit and its tree.\n\nPlanner direction for the fix: send filter blob:none with deepen 1 in the one-object v2 fetch. The pack then holds the wanted commit and its trees, without blobs. Keep the wanted object and bound the pack by the existing byte limits instead of a one-object closure. Keep the response guard as it is. Add this exact 400 text as a test specimen. The planner deploys the approved head and reads the next tail.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}